cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MINT: the Muon Induced Neutrino Tool"
message: "If you use MINT in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hostert
    given-names: Matheus
    email: matheus-hostert@uiowa.edu
    affiliation: University of Iowa
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Joel
repository-code: "https://github.com/jchoi55/MINT"
url: "https://github.com/jchoi55/MINT"
abstract: >-
  MINT simulates neutrino fluxes at muon facilities. It decays muons along a
  realistic accelerator lattice, taken from a MAD-X TWISS table, keeping the
  beam optics, muon polarization, and NLO decay corrections, and propagates the
  resulting neutrinos to a detector.
keywords:
  - physics
  - neutrino
  - muon collider
  - simulation
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
